1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,330
Hey guys,

2
00:00:01,610 --> 00:00:02,870
SuperHorrorBroMike here,

3
00:00:02,990 --> 00:00:11,070
and in today's video we journey through a haunted dreamscape as we explain the story and ending of Little Nightmares 3.

4
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:16,930
So sit back, relax, and let's dive into a world full of monsters and mystery.

5
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,510
Just as with Little Nightmares 1 and 2,

6
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:32,970
the third entry in this chilling horror franchise takes place in a dream dimension known as the Nowhere,

7
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:37,510
within a land called The Spiral, where the game's many locations are set.

8
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:41,150
Where Little Nightmares 1 followed the story of Six,

9
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:45,610
the sequel followed her again in addition to new character Mono.

10
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:51,110
This third title instead opts to introduce two brand new pint -sized heroes,

11
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:55,330
a little girl named Alone, and a boy called Lowe.

12
00:00:55,690 --> 00:01:00,070
Alone is able to use her wrench as both a weapon for whacking enemies,

13
00:01:00,410 --> 00:01:03,210
breaking down walls, and solving various puzzles.

14
00:01:03,870 --> 00:01:08,330
Lo, meanwhile, comes equipped with a bow and uses it to shoot at enemies,

15
00:01:08,670 --> 00:01:11,510
sever frayed ropes, and jam up gears.

16
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:19,990
Our two plucky adventurers often using their combined skillset to work together in order to progress through each stage.

17
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:25,750
Just as Six had the power to sap the life force from other beings in order to grow stronger,

18
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:29,370
and Mono was able to harness the signal tower's transmission, mission,

19
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:34,910
using it to move through television sets and bend the very fabric of time to his will,

20
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:42,110
Lo also possesses a unique ability, allowing him to travel through mirrors, taking alone with him.

21
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:47,830
This is how the duo move from one location to the next as they progress through their adventure.

22
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:49,790
With the basics explained,

23
00:01:50,090 --> 00:01:56,170
let's dive into the story itself as we take a look at each location and the enemies found within them.

24
00:01:56,650 --> 00:02:04,730
The The Necropolis is a sprawling

25
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:09,410
desert wasteland in which the ruins of an ancient civilization now stand.

26
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:13,310
This is a ghost town with no survivors to be found.

27
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:18,870
Crows feed on the corpses of the townsfolk who have been frozen in place by a giant,

28
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:21,590
lumbering doll known as Monster Baby.

29
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:28,570
The Baby uses a spotlight emanating from its eyes to turn any living being to stone in seconds.

30
00:02:28,570 --> 00:02:33,190
It's not a good place to be, but unfortunately for our two heroes,

31
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:39,730
this is where they awake, beside a broken mirror it seems they recently used to travel through.

32
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:44,550
As Low comes to, he is helped up by his companion alone,

33
00:02:44,850 --> 00:02:47,410
and quickly whips out what seems to be a map.

34
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:53,750
This map is used as a navigation point, so the pair can locate another mirror and escape through it.

35
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:54,870
The objective?

36
00:02:55,230 --> 00:02:59,970
To discover that one elusive looking glass that will break them free of the nowhere for good

37
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:04,290
and return the duo to the waking world known as the Counties.

38
00:03:04,850 --> 00:03:09,670
As the pair venture out into the desert ahead, we notice a curious sight.

39
00:03:10,010 --> 00:03:12,770
It seems this desert was once a great ocean,

40
00:03:12,970 --> 00:03:19,830
and the place the pair awoke inside was The Maw the Maw was the giant ship the original game took place on.

41
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:21,550
If this theory is correct,

42
00:03:21,870 --> 00:03:27,510
then it would place the events of Little Nightmares 3 far ahead of prior titles in the series.

43
00:03:27,930 --> 00:03:30,670
It gives us a good indication of the timeline.

44
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:34,630
After scaling the Great Wall and entering the city,

45
00:03:34,970 --> 00:03:40,470
Lone and Alone begin to explore their surroundings, working together to traverse the dangers ahead.

46
00:03:40,910 --> 00:03:46,710
It isn't long before they encounter a giant hand, buried beneath a pile of rubble.

47
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:51,710
Sadly, this hand doesn't belong to a corpse, but rather the resting monster baby,

48
00:03:51,910 --> 00:03:54,890
who then wakes and begins roaming the city streets.

49
00:03:56,220 --> 00:04:01,040
For now, Lo and Alone remain undetected and so push forward.

50
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:04,340
They come across a pair of feather umbrellas,

51
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:10,940
and use these very fashionable accessories to ascend upwards by harnessing wind rushing through The grates.

52
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:14,060
the umbrellas also come in handy when falling,

53
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:18,720
allowing the children to gradually descend rather than fall to their death.

54
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:23,810
As they continue through the ruined buildings, the kids come across black eggs.

55
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:27,370
Sometimes these eggs are stuffed inside bodies of the dead,

56
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:33,750
and others laid in various corridors and crawl spaces, squishing satisfyingly underfoot.

57
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:37,570
It's not long before we discover who these eggs belong to,

58
00:04:37,730 --> 00:04:40,790
as the duo encounter a nest of giant beetles,

59
00:04:40,850 --> 00:04:44,190
who have eyes on making Lo and alone their next meal.

60
00:04:44,850 --> 00:04:47,710
Lo must shoot down these winged pests with his bow,

61
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:52,370
and then Alone quickly rushes over to smash them to pulp using her wrench.

62
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:57,000
Monster Baby relentlessly pursues our heroes through the city,

63
00:04:57,320 --> 00:05:01,220
attempting to grab them and turn them to stone with its spotlight.

64
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:05,820
Eventually Lo and alone come face to face with the giant doll,

65
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:10,440
and with nowhere to run, it grabs them and drops them into the void.

66
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,500
Lo

67
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,500
Lo then

68
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,740
wakes in his bed.

69
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:37,920
He no longer wears his mask or cape and finds himself in a creepy padded cell.

70
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:40,020
Was this all just a nightmare?

71
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:42,220
And where is he now?

72
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:46,460
On the bed we can see various drawings that Lo has sketched,

73
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:49,020
they seem to be of locations we are yet to visit.

74
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:52,000
Someone then begins to approach the door,

75
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:56,900
and fearing this mysterious visitor, Lo takes refuge beneath the bed.

76
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:11,490
Lo then wakes back in the Necropolis,

77
00:06:11,870 --> 00:06:15,790
buried under a pile of debris after seemingly surviving his fall.

78
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:20,370
Alone is also still alive, helping Lo up and handing over his map.

79
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:25,170
Nighttime has set in, and the city takes on a far creepier atmosphere.

80
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:29,990
The two children come across a series of mysterious chalk drawings,

81
00:06:30,450 --> 00:06:36,250
which seem to depict a giant hand with an eye attached, a gong, and a selection of mirrors.

82
00:06:36,850 --> 00:06:42,450
While this may seem random, it is in fact a foreshadowing of future events.

83
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:44,050
More on that later.

84
00:06:44,470 --> 00:06:47,850
Despite the late hour, Monster Baby is not sleeping,

85
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:51,270
and stands as a continuous roadblock in our path ahead.

86
00:06:51,810 --> 00:06:57,390
Lo and Alone must come up with inventive ways to move the doll out of their way and sneak past,

87
00:06:57,730 --> 00:07:01,570
such as this sequence where they ring an enormous bell in a bell tower,

88
00:07:01,850 --> 00:07:06,510
causing the baby to tear it down and wander off to play with their new toy.

89
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,940
Eventually they run out of places to hide,

90
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:45,800
ambushed by Monster Baby who proceeds to lift up the building they are in and desperately search for the terrified children,

91
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:50,220
who take cover behind various objects that remain still standing.

92
00:07:50,890 --> 00:07:56,030
Just as it seems their luck has run out, a murder of crows show up to save the day,

93
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:59,050
swarming Monster Baby and pecking at its head,

94
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:02,230
causing the hulking beast to retreat into the horizon.

95
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:08,190
With the danger now past, they push on, and Lo locates the mirror from his map.

96
00:08:08,410 --> 00:08:11,650
He places his palm to the glass and takes a loan by the hand,

97
00:08:11,870 --> 00:08:16,950
the two then pulled inside, fleeing the dangers of the necropolis.

98
00:08:23,930 --> 00:08:30,400
Lowe emerges in a damp and dirty ventilation room in what appears to be a more industrial locale.

99
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:34,340
A lone follows shortly behind, breaking the mirror behind her.

100
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:40,760
There's no going back now, as Lowe cannot travel through glass surfaces that are cracked or broken.

101
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:44,320
The next stage of their journey is set within a candy factory,

102
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:48,020
although you probably wouldn't want to eat the sweets being manufactured here.

103
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:51,420
As the kids explore they see vast production lines,

104
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:56,560
where obese workers are hoisted along cables on winches from one job to the next.

105
00:08:57,060 --> 00:09:01,640
The main antagonist of this stage is the overseer of Candy Production,

106
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:06,320
a spidery lady with six arms known as the Supervisor.

107
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:12,400
A haunting grin that stretches ear to ear like a Cheshire cat plastered across her face.

108
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:19,060
Lohan alone must use stealth to avoid detection as the Supervisor goes about her daily tasks,

109
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:19,200
risks,

110
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:25,820
which include filing paperwork and monitoring the many security cameras found throughout the factory.

111
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:30,640
In time, they are discovered by the supervisor, who gives chase.

112
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:44,670
Lone and Alone plummet down through the factory after pushing through a vent,

113
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:49,990
but luckily are saved by Annette and fortunately placed a pile of sweet treats.

114
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:54,670
The next threat the pair encounter are flesh -eating bugs,

115
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:57,450
who swarm various rooms throughout the factory.

116
00:09:57,950 --> 00:10:01,030
This place seriously needs better pest control.

117
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:07,390
The only way to evade these killer creepy crawlies is to turn on the lights, or failing that,

118
00:10:07,650 --> 00:10:11,570
use a light source such as this power cell to keep them at arm's length.

119
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:16,490
These bugs hate luminance, and scurry away at the very sight of it.

120
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:20,410
After some more exploring and puzzle solving,

121
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:24,250
Loan alone come face to face with the supervisor Visor once more.

122
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:27,470
This time, she takes on a new, disturbing appearance,

123
00:10:27,950 --> 00:10:32,310
removing the lower half of her body and crawling around like a spider.

124
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:36,550
This new form grants the arachnid monster better mobility,

125
00:10:36,910 --> 00:10:40,210
allowing her to travel up walls and move at greater speed.

126
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:44,210
She chases the kids through the factory at every turn,

127
00:10:44,430 --> 00:10:47,850
eventually culminating in a breathless sequence,

128
00:10:47,870 --> 00:10:53,390
where she finally meets a gruesome demise thanks to Lo and Alone's stellar teamwork.

129
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:17,070
With the supervisor now super -flattened,

130
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:20,970
our intrepid explorers push onwards in relative safety,

131
00:11:21,230 --> 00:11:23,970
locating the next mirror from the map.

132
00:11:24,490 --> 00:11:28,870
Lo takes Alone by the hand, and the two travel to their next destination.

133
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:39,020
The mirror spits Lo out onto the floor of the storeroom,

134
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:42,620
but alone does not follow, at least not right away.

135
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:47,700
It takes a few moments before she emerges, smashing the mirror behind her.

136
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:52,740
She seems dead at first, with Lo shaking her unresponsively.

137
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,480
However, she is still alive, jolting awake,

138
00:11:56,840 --> 00:12:01,480
at which point Lo wraps his arms around her in a relieved, loving embrace.

139
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:07,340
Whether they will survive this next chapter in their adventure is another matter entirely.

140
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:11,000
The third stage is set within a bustling carnival,

141
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:16,540
full of brutish monsters who resemble the guests seen in the original Little Nightmares.

142
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:20,540
We see these patrons engaging in various morbid activities,

143
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:25,680
such as beating a lifeless corpse stuffed with candy as if it was a pinata.

144
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:31,380
The carnival stage sees the return of a fan favourite character, the gnomes.

145
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:36,080
Once children now transformed into these cute, curious critters,

146
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:41,560
the gnomes scamper about from hiding spot to hiding spot as Lone and Alone track them down.

147
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:47,680
And just like in Little Nightmares 1, we can give them big hugs when they eventually settle down.

148
00:12:48,690 --> 00:12:53,210
Our heroes follow these gnomes through the haunting halls of the carnival's underbelly,

149
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:56,690
and it is here we encounter the first enemy of the stage,

150
00:12:56,690 --> 00:13:02,590
age, living puppets with freaky looking face masks that seem to be made from human skin.

151
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:07,970
In order to thwart the puppets, Lo must first shoot their heads off with his bow,

152
00:13:08,190 --> 00:13:11,190
allowing Alone to follow up with a strike from her wrench,

153
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:14,550
which finally takes the still, lumbering bodies down,

154
00:13:14,910 --> 00:13:18,650
Lo baiting the body to follow him while she does so.

155
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:35,650
After leaving the underbelly, the children emerge on the surface above,

156
00:13:36,010 --> 00:13:38,330
and begin to navigate through the funfair.

157
00:13:38,530 --> 00:13:42,910
There's not much fun to be had here though, as danger looms at every turn.

158
00:13:43,310 --> 00:13:46,270
There's also some decidedly morbid sights.

159
00:13:46,710 --> 00:13:52,670
In one moment we're dropping a still -living chained resident into a dunking tank in order to progress,

160
00:13:53,110 --> 00:13:54,890
drowning them in the process.

161
00:13:55,290 --> 00:13:56,310
And in the next,

162
00:13:56,330 --> 00:14:02,250
we're pulling apart a sawn -through corpse in a magician's box so the duo can access us a hard -to -reach window.

163
00:14:02,970 --> 00:14:04,690
It's pretty macabre stuff.

164
00:14:06,110 --> 00:14:10,230
Eventually, the pair locate a rollercoaster ride and set it in motion,

165
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:17,030
boarding the carriage as it twists and turns through a haunted house and tears through the carnival at lightning speed.

166
00:14:17,490 --> 00:14:20,390
When the coaster finally reaches the end of the line,

167
00:14:20,550 --> 00:14:24,050
the two disembark and come across the next mirror on the map.

168
00:14:24,410 --> 00:14:26,910
However, there's a wrinkle in their plan.

169
00:14:27,250 --> 00:14:33,230
This mirror is now broken, meaning there's no way for Lo to use his power to travel through it.

170
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,420
Lo seems defeated.

171
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:40,700
Without the mirror, both he and Alone will remain trapped in the nowhere forever.

172
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:48,000
Alone is more optimistic, picking up the map and encouraging her friend not to give up hope.

173
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:52,220
Moving on they encounter the main antagonist of this chapter,

174
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:58,260
a horrifying puppeteer with a mangled face and living puppet companion known as The Kin.

175
00:14:58,540 --> 00:15:05,160
His puppet simply named Kin Junior, so I'll just refer to him as Junior from this point forward.

176
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:09,620
The Kin and his pet have fallen asleep in front of the television set,

177
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:12,780
allowing Lo and Alone to edge past unnoticed.

178
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,580
Unfortunately, the path ahead is boarded up,

179
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:20,780
and pulling these boards down makes enough racket to wake both Kin and Junior,

180
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,900
who instantly give chase.

181
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:24,140
The

182
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:48,860
The two

183
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:49,280
children

184
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:52,280
manage to evade the mad puppeteer on this occasion,

185
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,460
however it isn't long before Junior locates them,

186
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:58,800
forcing Lo and Alone to take safety inside an elevator.

187
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:01,680
This reprieve is short -lived,

188
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:05,960
as they come face to face with the Kin upon its arrival at the floor above.

189
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:11,860
The Kin snatches up Lo, but Alone manages to escape his clutches.

190
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:16,990
However, unlike Six, who would never put her life at risk to save another,

191
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:21,450
Alone is loyal to her friend Lo, and so enacts a jailbreak.

192
00:16:22,230 --> 00:16:27,910
Lo has been caged high up in the Kin's quarters, and the two must work as a team if he is to escape.

193
00:16:28,410 --> 00:16:32,230
Lo shoots arrows at objects around the environment to distract the Kin,

194
00:16:32,410 --> 00:16:37,050
while Alone sneaks over to a winch in order to move the cage closer to a ladder,

195
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:41,870
allowing her to jump up and down on the cage until it comes crashing to the floor.

196
00:16:42,550 --> 00:16:45,450
With the kin distracted by a now -free gnome,

197
00:16:45,570 --> 00:16:49,070
the duo continue moving forward in search of safe haven.

198
00:16:49,410 --> 00:16:53,350
They come into contact with the puppeteer several more times.

199
00:16:53,710 --> 00:16:56,170
In this scene we see the children captured

200
00:16:56,170 --> 00:17:02,650
by this psychopath are made to perform circus tricks for his amusement as he watches with sinister glee.

201
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,980
This culminates in a chase sequence,

202
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:10,680
where the Kin and Junior pursue Lo and Alone through the halls of the theatre,

203
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:13,100
and then through the carnival stalls.

204
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:30,000
The

205
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:40,800
The

206
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,020
kids eventually discover

207
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:45,020
a hot air balloon and rise into the skies above.

208
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:49,580
The Kin attempts to shoot it down with a shotgun, but is unsuccessful.

209
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,720
However, his puppet pal Junior Jr.

210
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:57,160
manages to scamper up the side of the balloon and attempts to drop down from above.

211
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:03,740
Lo and Alone quickly pull the burner valve, incinerating the nasty creature in the process.

212
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:08,100
The balloon takes them high above the carnival and across a lake,

213
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:10,920
but as the storm around them picks up,

214
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:16,180
a bolt of lightning hits the top of the balloon, causing it to plummet downwards.

215
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:20,820
At that moment, Lo wakes back up in his prison.

216
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:26,080
On the bed beside him, off three sketches of the locations he and Alone have visited.

217
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:30,760
Lo hears the footsteps of a mysterious visitor outside his room,

218
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:34,020
and so hurriedly hides his sketches in a garbage chute.

219
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:39,800
He hides underneath the bed until danger has passed, and then reopens The chute.

220
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:44,060
the drawings spill back out, along with something curious.

221
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:49,840
A small doll that bears a striking resemblance to that of alone.

222
00:18:57,200 --> 00:19:03,180
Returning to the Nowhere, we discover both our plucky heroes survived the crash landing unscathed.

223
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:05,720
As the two take in their surroundings,

224
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:10,640
they realise they have crash landed on the shoreline beside a mysterious building.

225
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:13,080
This is the Institution.

226
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:21,100
The Institution is an asylum -like structure used in the real world to treat children suffering from trauma.

227
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:25,420
It is featured in The podcast series the Sounds of Nightmares,

228
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:31,680
and there are in fact many references both big and small to that series in Little Nightmares 3.

229
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:37,640
However, as listeners of the podcast will be aware, the Institute was far from innocent.

230
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,780
It was run by a therapist by the name of Otto.

231
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:47,860
Otto was once a kind and well -meaning doctor, seeking to help the children under his care.

232
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:48,500
However,

233
00:19:49,020 --> 00:19:52,000
he is led down a dark path after suspecting

234
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:58,700
that the disappearance of his kid sister Cece may have been tied to a mysterious figure known as the Ferryman,

235
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:02,040
who many of his patients encountered in their dreams.

236
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:08,810
night in my dream a muddled voice and then I

237
00:20:09,260 --> 00:20:14,480
saw him there must be more try interact with the dream

238
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:21,030
scream tearing my throat but you

239
00:20:21,030 --> 00:20:24,050
were right there don't tell me you did nothing You're

240
00:20:24,050 --> 00:20:25,010
supposed to help me!

241
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:26,290
You're supposed to understand!

242
00:20:26,830 --> 00:20:27,230
I

243
00:20:27,230 --> 00:20:29,410
can't help you if you hide things from me!

244
00:20:29,570 --> 00:20:30,130
My head!

245
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:32,300
A fire burns in there!

246
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:32,600
We

247
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,520
can face your monsters together!

248
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:35,760
Please stop!

249
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:36,280
Otto

250
00:20:37,750 --> 00:20:41,350
became obsessed with trying to connect to the nowhere.

251
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:45,930
He used sleep therapy by drugging his patients with spiked

252
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:52,330
candy so he can monitor their nightmares and then interview them about their visits to the nowhere in search of answers.

253
00:20:52,810 --> 00:20:55,890
Everything ties back to the sounds of nightmares.

254
00:20:57,430 --> 00:21:02,650
Here in this nightmare realm, the Institute takes on a far more sinister vibe,

255
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:09,390
dilapidated and full of monstrous creatures who want nothing more than to sap the life from low and alone.

256
00:21:09,910 --> 00:21:14,490
We also discover the spirits of the children who once lived here as patients,

257
00:21:14,810 --> 00:21:18,490
now living on as ghostly echoes of the past.

258
00:21:19,910 --> 00:21:25,710
In terms of enemies, we have the staff, nurses with bandaged faces covering their eyes.

259
00:21:26,050 --> 00:21:31,890
This does at least allow our heroes to be able to sneak past of them most of the time, Failing that,

260
00:21:31,930 --> 00:21:37,270
a loud distraction such as throwing a can or bottle across the room can be used to thwart their advances.

261
00:21:38,110 --> 00:21:40,210
Next up we have the killer plants.

262
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:43,550
Now these plants detect nearby movement and then

263
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:49,190
spit out a long tendril that grabs hold of and kills anything unlucky enough to get too close.

264
00:21:49,910 --> 00:21:56,110
In this sequence we can even use one of said plants to take care of one of those pesky nurses.

265
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:18,750
The final enemy we encounter is a giant doctor with long arms and legs that twist and turn through the halls of The asylum.

266
00:22:19,210 --> 00:22:22,250
the doctor in question may actually be Otto,

267
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:25,850
which would suggest he eventually committed enough heinous

268
00:22:25,850 --> 00:22:31,270
acts against the children under his care at the Institute to garner the attention of the Nowhere.

269
00:22:31,550 --> 00:22:39,750
This monstrous form is probably not what Otto had intended for himself on his quest to enter the realm that took his beloved sister.

270
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:44,120
But before we get to Otto and his encounter with Lo and Alone,

271
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:50,840
let's rewind a little and look at some of the other key plot points we uncover while exploring this creepy locale.

272
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:55,620
The biggest twist comes with the discovery of a very familiar room.

273
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:58,340
Lo and Alone enter a padlock cell,

274
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:04,680
which is an exact match for the one Lo awakens within at certain points in our adventure.

275
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:08,740
This discovery tells us that Lo was a patient of the Institute,

276
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:14,140
and the mysterious visitor who comes to his door each night was almost certainly Otto,

277
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:16,500
monitoring his sleep patterns.

278
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:21,810
Inside the garbage chute we discover the doll that resembles a loan.

279
00:23:22,170 --> 00:23:27,450
It is carried over into the nowhere, but here it has a mysterious superpower.

280
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:34,470
After picking up the doll, Lo is able to carry it around and alter a small area around him.

281
00:23:34,750 --> 00:23:41,330
The doll's aura transforms the environment to return to the way it was in the waking world of the counties.

282
00:23:41,930 --> 00:23:44,410
Doors that were once closed now open.

283
00:23:45,030 --> 00:23:47,530
Surroundings are no longer in a state of ruin,

284
00:23:47,670 --> 00:23:51,790
and even this broken goldfish bowl returns to its previous state,

285
00:23:52,010 --> 00:23:54,650
aquatic denizens still alive and kicking.

286
00:23:54,650 --> 00:24:00,080
Low uses the doll to help him and Alone travel deeper inside the Institute.

287
00:24:00,540 --> 00:24:04,940
Along the way, they encounter Otto's stretchy arms blocking their path.

288
00:24:05,260 --> 00:24:09,720
To move him out of the way, Alone must use her wrench to ring a series of gongs,

289
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:14,340
sending ripples throughout the environment and disturbing the Doctor's slumber.

290
00:24:14,940 --> 00:24:18,280
Otto's hands feature eyes in the centre of their palms.

291
00:24:18,620 --> 00:24:20,640
If any of this sounds familiar,

292
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:27,320
cast your mind back to that cryptic series of chalk scratchings we encountered while exploring the necropolis.

293
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:30,240
Indeed, they foreshadowed the endgame.

294
00:24:31,020 --> 00:24:36,580
After a series of breakneck chases where Lowe and Alone narrowly escape the Doctor's grasp,

295
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:40,260
they eventually reach a room with the mirror from Lowe's dreams.

296
00:24:40,620 --> 00:24:45,140
A mirror which will allow them to escape the nowhere spiral for good.

297
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:52,140
But as Lowe places his hand on the glass one last time, Alonne seems reluctant to follow.

298
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:57,980
She holds back, and in doing so buys Otto enough time to catch up with them,

299
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:02,480
at which point he snatches away the mirror and begins tearing down the room.

300
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:06,860
Our heroes must evade falling debris until a set of gongs appear,

301
00:25:07,220 --> 00:25:12,900
at which point Alonne rings them causing the doctor's palms to open and reveal its eye.

302
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:19,840
Lowe then shoots the eye, causing the hand to become immobile and crushed under falling rubble.

303
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:23,620
After doing this twice, Otto shows his face,

304
00:25:23,740 --> 00:25:27,160
and the kids are able to take him down once and for all.

305
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:28,040
As

306
00:25:57,600 --> 00:25:58,400
As the

307
00:25:58,400 --> 00:25:59,820
doctor falls to his death,

308
00:26:00,020 --> 00:26:02,060
he smashes the floor in front of him,

309
00:26:02,220 --> 00:26:04,700
causing Lowe and Alone to plummet down with him.

310
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:10,000
They land on a crumbling ledge, alone saving Lo from falling further.

311
00:26:10,380 --> 00:26:13,860
But as the ledge gives way, they continue their descent,

312
00:26:14,220 --> 00:26:18,820
embracing one another as they fall, friends to the very end.

313
00:26:25,650 --> 00:26:28,980
Low Lo wakes in his bed inside the asylum once more.

314
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:32,640
This time, he is holding the doll of Alone in his arms,

315
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:37,160
just as he was moments earlier as the pair fell into the void below.

316
00:26:37,620 --> 00:26:43,560
He sets the Alone doll down on the bed and goes over to the garbage chute to gather up his sketches and crayons.

317
00:26:43,840 --> 00:26:48,400
As he returns to the bed, Alone is now sitting in place of her doll.

318
00:26:48,780 --> 00:26:51,680
The two settle down and begin to draw together.

319
00:26:53,060 --> 00:26:56,360
We then transition back to the ruins of the institute,

320
00:26:56,700 --> 00:27:02,220
where miraculously the two children have survived, and thankfully, the doctor has not.

321
00:27:03,060 --> 00:27:04,380
Battered and bruised,

322
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:10,380
they pick themselves up and begin to hobble through the crumbling building in search of that one last mirror.

323
00:27:10,840 --> 00:27:15,540
The mirror is thankfully still intact, landing just ahead of them.

324
00:27:16,220 --> 00:27:21,200
Lo places his palm on the surface of the looking glass and takes a loan by the hand,

325
00:27:21,420 --> 00:27:23,600
but once again she pulls away.

326
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:26,400
Lo insists on taking her with him,

327
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:31,280
saving her from this nightmare realm and bringing her back to the safety of the counties.

328
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:36,180
Reluctantly, she takes his hand, and the two are dragged through the portal.

329
00:27:36,620 --> 00:27:42,780
However, moments later, Alone is spat back out of the mirror, which then shatters behind her.

330
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:46,160
Not only was she unable to travel with Lowe,

331
00:27:46,340 --> 00:27:52,560
but she also begins to vanish in his absence, her empty clothes falling to the floor.

332
00:28:13,770 --> 00:28:18,210
A post -credits sequence finds Lowe back in the waking world,

333
00:28:18,450 --> 00:28:21,430
but this time not in his cell within the Institute.

334
00:28:21,870 --> 00:28:27,630
It seems he has returned home, or at least to the ruins of a place that was once his home.

335
00:28:27,890 --> 00:28:34,150
This tells us that certain children can find ways to escape the Nowhere after entering it,

336
00:28:34,250 --> 00:28:36,710
and Lo is now safe from the terrors within.

337
00:28:37,230 --> 00:28:42,190
However, he seems desperate to return and reunite with his lost friend,

338
00:28:42,470 --> 00:28:47,090
and so begins the laborious task of piecing the glass back together.

339
00:28:47,770 --> 00:28:50,890
So, what does this ending actually mean?

340
00:28:51,170 --> 00:28:53,230
Well, it's simple enough to explain.

341
00:28:54,010 --> 00:28:56,190
As we established at the beginning of this video,

342
00:28:56,570 --> 00:29:00,470
children within the Nowhere usually seem to possess certain powers.

343
00:29:00,890 --> 00:29:07,110
However, unlike Low, Six and Mono, Alone never had a power of her own.

344
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:11,090
She also only ever appeared in the waking world as a doll,

345
00:29:11,310 --> 00:29:16,230
and seemed to be an imaginary friend of Lo's to give him comfort while imprisoned.

346
00:29:16,840 --> 00:29:21,140
But, upon travelling to the Nowhere, which is essentially a dream world,

347
00:29:21,340 --> 00:29:25,880
that imaginary friend manifested as a living, breathing child.

348
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:29,300
Alone very much existed in Lo's mind,

349
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:33,660
and so was made just as real as him when he visited the Nowhere.

350
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:40,480
But, as soon as Lo broke free of that world, his imaginary friend alone no longer could exist,

351
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:44,080
as his tether to that realm has now been severed.

352
00:29:44,260 --> 00:29:48,000
This suggests that the powers these children possess are

353
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:54,680
in fact a product of their subconscious brought to life via the very existence of travelling to a dreamlike dimension,

354
00:29:55,120 --> 00:29:59,840
and it helps us understand how the world of Little Nightmares actually works.

355
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:04,440
of course, some Of these concepts are pure speculation on my part,

356
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,920
but there is a lot of evidence to support it.

357
00:30:08,180 --> 00:30:13,880
Either way, Alone is now no more, and while Lo escaped his nightmare,

358
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:17,340
he sadly lost his best friend in the process.

359
00:30:20,170 --> 00:30:21,450
And with that,

360
00:30:21,450 --> 00:30:26,770
we come to the end of this video and a look at the story of Little Nightmares 3 Explained.

361
00:30:26,910 --> 00:30:31,570
I hope you enjoyed this video and found it both entertaining and informative.

362
